## Project test style

General rules — `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/presets/python/tests.md`: test layout mirrors the code
structure · the test name names a scenario, not a module · the docstring states the behavior · next to
"it worked" sits the counter-case "and this must not work" · data comes through factories · a fake is an explicit
class, not `Mock` · a dependency is replaced via DI, not `monkeypatch`.

This project's code and test practices are in `.retainer/practices.md` (template —
`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/presets/practices.md.template`): `code-reviewer` reads them on the diff,
